  "id": "recovery",
  "term": "recovery",
  "definition": "Recovery is a changing process in which lost function improves over time through biological repair, reorganization of remaining systems, and gradual improvement in behavior or performance. In the source context of post-stroke aphasia, this progression unfolds across linked stages from early neural recovery to later compensatory changes and behavioral gains.",
